                    \begin {tikzcd}                     A(F(x), -) \ar [d, Rightarrow, "≀", "πₓ"'] & A(F(y), -) \ar [d, Rightarrow, "≀"', "π_y"]\ar [l, Rightarrow, "-∘\overline {F}(f)"'] \\
                        X(x, U(-)) & X(y, U(-)) \ar [l, Rightarrow, "-∘f"]
                    \end {tikzcd}
                ]]></fr:embedded-tex-body></fr:embedded-tex></fr:mainmatter><fr:backmatter /></fr:tree>
            Then clearly <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[∃!\overline {F}.∀f : X(x, y). \overline {F}(f) = よ⁻¹(πₓ⁻¹∘(-∘f)∘π_y)]]></fr:tex>.
        </fr:li>

        <fr:li>
            (dual) Suppose such a <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[\overline {U}]]></fr:tex> exists.
            Then naturality of <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[π]]></fr:tex> requires that
            <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[∀u : A(a, b).]]></fr:tex> this square in <fr:tex
display="inline"><![CDATA[Set^{Xᵒᵖ}]]></fr:tex> commutes:
            <fr:tree
